        {
          "source_quote": "ὅθεν ἀθανασίας ἐπικρατούσης εὐλόγως πάντα γεγονότα φανήσεται.",
          "english_quote": "Hence, when immortality prevails, it will become apparent that everything has come into being with good reason.",
          "issue": "The draft attaches εὐλόγως to the coming into being expressed by γεγονότα, producing a claim about the rationale of everything’s origin. That is defensible in the surrounding discussion of the usefulness and suitability of created things. However, εὐλόγως can instead qualify φανήσεται, expressing the reasonableness of the appearance or inference. This material attachment alternative is not disclosed in the notes.",
          "suggested_revision": "Add a source-quoted note explaining that the main text reads εὐλόγως with γεγονότα, “has come into being with good reason,” because the surrounding argument discusses the purposes of things. Preserve the alternative attachment to φανήσεται, approximately “it will reasonably appear that everything has come into being.” Do not present either attachment as uniquely established. Submit the amended passage and note for fresh review.",
          "severity": "major"
        }
      ]
    }
